CASE 5: MICROSERVICES ARCHITECTURE WITH A LAYER-7 LOAD BALANCER (WITHOUT A DEDICATED API GATEWAY)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek microservices architecture hai jisme multiple services hain:

    - User Service
    - Order Service
    - Payment Service

Har service ke multiple instances different servers par run kar rahe hain.

In services ke traffic ko handle karne ke liye ek Layer-7 (Application
Layer) Load Balancer use kiya ja raha hai. Ye URL / Path based routing
support karta hai.

Is architecture me separate API Gateway mandatory nahi hai — relatively
simple applications me L7 LB khud hi incoming requests ko appropriate
backend service tak route kar sakta hai.


Example Routing Rules:

    /users/**     →  User Service
    /orders/**    →  Order Service
    /payments/**  →  Payment Service


